---
import { type ProblemStatementProps } from '../../types/components';

interface Props extends ProblemStatementProps {}
const { id = "problem" } = Astro.props;
---

<section id={id} class="bg-white py-12 lg:py-24">
  <div class="section-container">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-8 leading-tight">
        Rigorous technical analysis — not a compliance checkbox
      </h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-8">
        Conventional technical reviews confirm what has been disclosed. They rarely test whether what remains undisclosed is already material to execution, financing, or investment timing.
        <br/><br/>
        BiP Omega applies a structured analytical process to identify those gaps — regardless of the source materials available.
      </p>

      <div class="bg-slate-50 p-6 lg:p-8 rounded-sm border border-slate-200 text-sm">
        <p class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 text-base">Representative example: a utility-scale BESS project appeared commercially mature on paper:</p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 mb-6">
          <li class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="text-green-600 font-bold text-lg">✓</span> <span class="text-slate-700">CEQA environmental approval</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="text-green-600 font-bold text-lg">✓</span> <span class="text-slate-700">Signed utility PPA</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="text-green-600 font-bold text-lg">✓</span> <span class="text-slate-700">Conventional third-party technical review</span></li>
        </ul>
        
        <p class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 text-base">But the disclosed record still left core questions unanswered:</p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 mb-6">
          <li class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="text-red-500 font-bold text-lg">✗</span> <span class="text-slate-700">Thermal derating curves at 46°C ambient temperature</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="text-red-500 font-bold text-lg">✗</span> <span class="text-slate-700">Bridge structural capacity over irrigation canal (150+ ton MPT loads)</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="text-red-500 font-bold text-lg">✗</span> <span class="text-slate-700">UL9540A fire propagation test results</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="text-red-500 font-bold text-lg">✗</span> <span class="text-slate-700">BLM federal permitting timeline for gen-tie right-of-way (NEPA)</span></li>
        </ul>

        <div class="bg-red-50 p-4 border-l-4 border-red-500 mb-4">
          <p class="font-bold text-red-900">Result: documented execution exposure that would have justified earlier technical caution.</p>
        </div>
        
        <p class="text-slate-700 font-medium">
           BiP Omega is designed to identify this kind of documentary risk before or during deeper diligence begins.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-slate-400 italic border-t border-slate-200 pt-2">
           Illustrative example. Project details anonymized.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-sm shadow-sm border border-slate-100">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">The Compliance Trap</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Most technical reviews confirm what has been disclosed. They rarely test whether what remains undisclosed is already material to execution, resilience, or investment timing. BiP Omega identifies those omissions as Critical Silences.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-sm shadow-sm border border-slate-100">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Evidence-Based Gating</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-600 mb-6">
          To avoid false confidence, each finding is classified under explicit evidence discipline:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-slate-600 mb-8">
           <li class="flex gap-3">
             <span class="font-bold text-slate-900 min-w-[100px]">Verified:</span> 
             <span>Confirmed by independent tangible evidence</span>
           </li>
           <li class="flex gap-3">
             <span class="font-bold text-slate-900 min-w-[100px]">Assumed:</span> 
             <span>Industry-standard inference (flagged as unverified)</span>
           </li>
           <li class="flex gap-3">
             <span class="font-bold text-red-600 min-w-[100px]">Critical Silence:</span> 
             <span>Material omissions that may impair technical confidence, execution viability, insurance positioning, or commercial assumptions</span>
           </li>
        </ul>
        
        <div class="bg-slate-50 p-5 rounded-sm text-sm">
            <p class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3 border-b border-slate-200 pb-2">Example Critical Silence:</p>
            <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">A developer discloses headline MW, but omits energy duration, thermal derating behavior, and throughput or warranty-performance detail.</p>
            
            <p class="font-bold text-red-600 mb-2">Why it matters:</p>
            <div class="space-y-1 text-slate-700">
              <p><span class="font-semibold">Model assumption:</span> headline capacity performs as marketed</p>
              <p><span class="font-semibold">Technical reality:</span> performance may be constrained by undocumented thermal, warranty, or delivery limits</p>
              <div class="mt-2 pt-2 border-t border-slate-200 font-bold text-red-600">
                <p>Unvalidated revenue assumptions</p>
                <p>Potential execution and insurance exposure</p>
              </div>
            </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
